# Line-ending policy
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shell scripts MUST stay LF: install.sh / traefik.sh are run on Linux hosts
# (and install.sh via `curl | bash`). A CRLF would make bash choke on the
# shebang and on every `\r`-terminated token. Pin them so a Windows checkout
# (autocrlf) can never reintroduce CRLF into the committed blob.
*.sh        text eol=lf

# Config + compose files are read inside Linux containers -- keep them LF too.
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf
